## Stacked Line Series

The following example demonstrates the performance improvement of incremental grouping with stacked line charts. When using `applyTransaction()` with the new incremental grouping feature, the chart only processes new data points instead of regrouping all data. Compare the CPU usage between `updateDelta()` (full reprocessing) and `applyTransaction()` (incremental updates).

{% chartExampleRunner title="High Frequency Stacked Line" name="high-freq-stacked-line" type="generated" /%}

## Multiple Charts

The following example demonstrates high-frequency updates across multiple area charts, simulating a monitoring dashboard for multiple systems. Each chart displays system and user CPU load with data updating every 50ms when the feed is running.

{% chartExampleRunner title="High Frequency Multi-Chart" name="high-freq-multi-chart" type="generated" /%}

## High Volume Line Series

This example is tuned for high-volume datasets. It starts with 100,000 data points and can add or remove batches of 100 points at a time. Use the controls to compare the cost of full `updateDelta()` refreshes against incremental `applyTransaction()` updates while the data stream maintains a constant window size.

{% chartExampleRunner title="High Frequency High Volume" name="high-freq-high-volume" type="generated" /%}

## Random Updates

This example investigates the performance of `applyTransaction()` with randomized updates on large datasets. Unlike append/remove operations, this tests in-place value mutations where random data points are updated each tick. Compare the cost of incremental `applyTransaction({ update })` against full `updateDelta()` refreshes.

{% chartExampleRunner title="High Frequency Random Update" name="high-freq-random-update" type="generated" /%}

## Financial Charts

The following examples demonstrate high-frequency updates using the Financial Charts API (`AgCharts.createFinancialChart`). This uses the simplified financial chart options with built-in features like volume, navigator, range buttons, status bar, and zoom.

### Real-Time Data Feed

This example simulates a real-time data feed updating a financial chart with new datums.

{% chartExampleRunner title="High Frequency Financial Chart" name="high-freq-financial-chart" type="generated" /%}

### High Volume Financial Chart

This example tests high-volume datasets with 100,000 data points using the Financial Charts API. Compare the performance of `applyTransaction()` vs `updateDelta()` for rolling window updates.

{% chartExampleRunner title="High Volume Financial Chart" name="high-freq-financial-high-volume" type="generated" /%}

### Random Updates

This example investigates the performance of randomized updates on large financial chart datasets. Random datums are mutated each tick to test in-place value updates.

